            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0224" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.939/34a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-14T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 2, 3 p.m. Has Chinese Government removed embargo on food
                    exports to Siberia? If not, renew representations and telegraph result. It is
                    reported to the Department that Bolsheviks are retaliating.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
